  "final_message": "I haven't made any changes. Removing `channel` from the `OrderPlaced` event would break ARCH-4, so I stopped before editing.\n\n`src/core/events.ts:16` and `:50` put `channel` on the event. ARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume `OrderPlaced` from other repositories. Changes to it must be additive, and removals have to go through deprecation. \"No longer read\" is true for this service, but I can't tell whether those two consumers still read it.\n\nThe order model is separate, but the field is still required on input. `channel` is validated in `src/core/order.ts:124` and parsed in `src/api/requestParsing.ts:18`. Making it optional or removing it from `POST /orders` would affect callers. Removing it from the order model could also change the `GET /orders/{id}` response that web-storefront uses (ARCH-8). That depends on whether the response includes `channel`, and I haven't checked yet.\n\nHere are the options:\n\n1. **Deprecation path (my recommendation):**\n   - Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` on the event and keep populating it.\n   - Make it optional on `POST /orders` and in the order model.\n   - Confirm with the billing-service and analytics-ingest teams that they've stopped reading it.\n   - Remove it from the event in a later change.\n2. **Full removal now:** I do this across the code, tests and docs. That's only safe if you confirm both consumers don't use `channel` and web-storefront doesn't read it.\n3. **Order model only:** I remove it from the internal model and stop validating it, but keep emitting it on the event. For that, I'd need a value to put on the event, such as a default.\n\nWhich one do you want? If you choose option 2, tell me the consumers have been checked.",
